The detector event data layer with libc++ and on macOS:
- InDetRIO_OnTrack: __sincos() on macOS, where sincos() (a GNU extension) is missing;
- TrkAlignEvent: std::resetiosflags, which libstdc++ lets argument-dependent lookup find
  (its fmtflags is an enum in std) and libc++ does not (an unsigned integer);
- TrigT1CaloCalibConditions: a value-initialised vector iterator rather than one made from 0,
  which only libstdc++'s iterator accepts.

--- a/InnerDetector/InDetRecEvent/InDetRIO_OnTrack/src/TRT_DriftCircleOnTrack.cxx
+++ b/InnerDetector/InDetRecEvent/InDetRIO_OnTrack/src/TRT_DriftCircleOnTrack.cxx
@@ -21,6 +21,13 @@
 #include <memory>
 #include <ostream>
 #include <utility>
+
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+namespace {
+// sincos() is a GNU extension; macOS has __sincos()
+inline void sincos(double x, double* s, double* c) { __sincos(x, s, c); }
+}
+#endif
 
 InDet::TRT_DriftCircleOnTrack::TRT_DriftCircleOnTrack(
   const InDet::TRT_DriftCircle* RIO,
